{"id": "ed9d92cd-90a7-4a5c-abf3-21ac1a5bf7b5", "slug": "nexus-ready-player-one", "title": "NEXUS - Ready Player One", "description": "Nexus Ready Login Section is designed for authenticating users through a focused access flow. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for authentication screens in web products.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-staff-featured-2026-05-22\"\nname: \"NEXUS - Ready Player One\"\ndescription: \"Nexus Ready Login Section is designed for authenticating users through a focused access flow. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for authentication screens in web products.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#00F0FF\"\n  secondary: \"#FF007F\"\n  accent: \"#FF007F\"\n  background: \"#050010\"\n  surface: \"#E0E0E0\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Space Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"VT323\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Space Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# NEXUS - Ready Player One\nSource: Neuform staff featured templates. Author: Samnang Aing (@samnang). Views: 91; favorites: 7; remixes: 2.\nTags: login, animated, input, validation, effect, security.\n## Overview\nNexus Ready Login Section is designed for authenticating users through a focused access flow. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for authentication screens in web products.\n\nNexus Arcades High Scores Cheats Guild Login Ready Player One: Start. Power up your digital infrastructure. We architect high-performance, resilient experiences and robust code loops designed to help ambitious guilds do…\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Ready Player One: Start..\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #00F0FF, secondary #FF007F, accent #FF007F, background #050010, surface #E0E0E0, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Space Mono for display moments and VT323 for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use Space Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nAuthentication and CTA controls should preserve the source button hierarchy, input density, and focused conversion path.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n\n<html lang=\"en\">\n\n<head>\n\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n\n  <title>NEXUS - Ready Player One</title>\n\n\n\n  <!-- Google Fonts for Retro Vibe -->\n\n  <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n\n  <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n\n  <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=VT323&display=swap\"\n    rel=\"stylesheet\">\n\n  <!-- Tailwind CSS -->\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n\n\n\n  <!-- Iconify -->\n\n  <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n\n\n\n  <!-- GSAP & ScrollTrigger -->\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n\n  <!-- Matter.js -->\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/matter-js/0.19.0/matter.min.js\"></script>\n\n</head>\n\n<body\n  class=\"bg-[#050010] text-[#e0e0e0] font-['Space_Mono'] overflow-x-hidden selection:bg-[#ff007f] selection:text-white relative min-h-screen antialiased\">\n\n  <!-- Canvas Background Layer -->\n\n  <div class=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 pointer-events-none overflow-hidden\" style=\"opacity: 0.95;\">\n\n    <canvas id=\"pixel-canvas\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full\"></canvas>\n\n    <!-- CSS Scanline Overlay -->\n\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0\" style=\"\n\n        background: repeating-linear-gradient(\n\n          to bottom,\n\n          transparent,\n\n          transparent 3px,\n\n          rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65) 3px,\n\n          rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65) 6px\n\n        );\n\n        pointer-events: none;\n\n      \">\n\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Edge Vignette -->\n\n    <div class=\"absolute inset-0\" style=\"\n\n        background: radial-gradient(circle at center, transparent 40%, #050010 100%);\n\n        pointer-events: none;\n\n      \">\n\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Main Content Wrapper -->\n\n  <div class=\"relative z-10 flex flex-col min-h-screen\">\n\n\n\n    <!-- Header -->\n\n    <header class=\"w-full max-w-[90rem] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12 py-6 flex justify-between items-center\">\n\n      <!-- Logo -->\n\n      <a href=\"#\" class=\"flex items-center gap-3 group\">\n\n        <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:gamepad-linear\"\n          class=\"text-3xl text-[#00f0ff] transform group-hover:scale-110 group-hover:rotate-3 transition-transform duration-300\"\n          style=\"stroke-width: 1.5;\">\n\n        </iconify-icon>\n\n        <span class=\"text-3xl font-['VT323'] text-white tracking-tight uppercase group-hover:text-[#00f0ff] transition-colors duration-300\">\n\n          Nexus\n\n        </span>\n\n      </a>\n\n      <!-- Navigation -->\n\n      <nav class=\"hidden md:flex items-center gap-10\">\n\n        <a href=\"#\"\n          class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-400 hover:text-[#00f0ff] uppercase tracking-wide transition-colors\">\n\n          Arcades\n\n        </a>\n\n        <a href=\"#\"\n          class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-400 hover:text-[#ff007f] uppercase tracking-wide transition-colors\">\n\n          High Scores\n\n        </a>\n\n        <a href=\"#\"\n          class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-400 hover:text-[#00f0ff] uppercase tracking-wide transition-colors\">\n\n          Cheats\n\n        </a>\n\n        <a href=\"#\"\n          class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-400 hover:text-[#ff007f] uppercase tracking-wide transition-colors\">\n\n          Guild\n\n        </a>\n\n      </nav>\n\n      <!-- Header CTA -->\n\n      <a href=\"#\"\n        class=\"hidden sm:inline-flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-medium text-white border-2 border-gray-700 hover:border-[#00f0ff] hover:text-[#00f0ff] hover:shadow-[0_0_10px_rgba(0,240,255,0.3)] bg-[#050010] uppercase tracking-wide px-5 py-2 transition-all duration-300\">\n\n        Login\n\n      </a>\n\n    </header>\n\n    <!-- Hero Section -->\n\n    <main class=\"flex-1 w-full max-w-[90rem] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-12 flex items-center pt-10 pb-32\">\n\n      <div class=\"max-w-3xl relative z-10\">\n\n\n\n        <!-- Masked Reveal Title -->\n\n        <h1 id=\"hero-title\"\n          class=\"font-['VT323'] text-7xl md:text-8xl lg:text-[8rem] tracking-tight leading-[0.95] mb-8 uppercase text-white drop-shadow-[0_0_10px_rgba(255,255,255,0.2)]\">\n\n          <span class=\"word-collider\" style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n\n            <span class=\"reveal-word block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Ready</span>\n\n          </span>\n\n          <span class=\"word-collider\" style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n\n            <span class=\"reveal-word block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">Player</span>\n\n          </span>\n\n          <br class=\"hidden sm:block\" />\n\n          <span class=\"word-collider\" style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n\n            <span class=\"reveal-word block\" style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">One:</span>\n\n          </span>\n\n          <span class=\"word-collider\" style=\"overflow: hidden; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em;\">\n\n            <span\n\n              class=\"reveal-word block text-[#ff007f] drop-shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(255,0,127,0.5)]\"\n\n              style=\"transform: translateY(110%);\">\n\n              Start.\n\n            </span>\n\n          </span>\n\n        </h1>\n\n        <!-- Subtitle -->\n\n        <p class=\"text-base md:text-lg text-gray-400 max-w-2xl leading-loose mb-12 opacity-0\" id=\"hero-desc\">\n\n          Power up your digital infrastructure. We architect high-performance, resilient experiences and robust code\n          loops designed to help ambitious guilds dominate the leaderboard.\n\n        </p>\n\n        <!-- CTA Button -->\n\n        <div class=\"opacity-0\" id=\"hero-cta\">\n\n          <a href=\"#\"\n            class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-4 bg-[#050010] border-2 border-[#00f0ff] text-[#00f0ff] hover:bg-[#00f0ff] hover:text-[#050010] px-8 py-4 font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-widest transition-all duration-300 shadow-[0_0_15px_rgba(0,240,255,0.2)] hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(0,240,255,0.6)] group\">\n\n            Insert Coin\n\n            <iconify-icon icon=\"solar:round-alt-arrow-right-linear\"\n              class=\"text-2xl transform group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform\" style=\"stroke-width: 1.5;\">\n\n            </iconify-icon>\n\n          </a>\n\n        </div>\n\n      </div>\n\n    </main>\n\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Application Logic -->\n\n  <script>\n    // --- 1. GSAP Animations ---\n\n    gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n    gsap.to(\".reveal-word\", {\n\n      y: \"0%\",\n\n      duration: 1.0,\n\n      ease: \"power4.out\",\n\n      stagger: 0.15,\n\n      scrollTrigger: {\n\n        trigger: \"#hero-title\",\n\n        start: \"top 85%\",\n\n      },\n\n      onComplete: () => {\n\n        // Once the headline is visually in place, map invisible Matter.js bodies onto the words.\n\n        setTimeout(() => {\n\n          createWordColliders();\n\n          releaseDelayedWave();\n\n        }, 120);\n\n      }\n\n    });\n\n    gsap.to([\"#hero-desc\", \"#hero-cta\"], {\n\n      opacity: 1,\n\n      y: 0,\n\n      duration: 1,\n\n      ease: \"power3.out\",\n\n      stagger: 0.2,\n\n      delay: 0.8,\n\n      startAt: {\n\n        y: 20\n\n      },\n\n      scrollTrigger: {\n\n        trigger: \"#hero-title\",\n\n        start: \"top 85%\",\n\n      }\n\n    });\n\n    // --- 2. Matter.js Falling Pixel Cubes + Word Colliders + Settled Blink ---\n\n    const canvas = document.getElementById('pixel-canvas');\n\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: false });\n\n    const {\n\n      Engine,\n\n      World,\n\n      Bodies,\n\n      Body,\n\n      Runner,\n\n      Events,\n\n      Sleeping\n\n    } = Matter;\n\n    let width;\n\n    let height;\n\n    let engine;\n\n    let world;\n\n    let runner;\n\n    const blockSize = 30;\n\n    const blocks = [];\n\n    const boundaries = [];\n\n    const wordColliderBodies = [];\n\n    const delayedBodies = [];\n\n    let physicsActive = true;\n\n    let settleTimer = null;\n\n    let started = false;\n\n    let wordCollidersCreated = false;\n\n    let delayedWaveReleased = false;\n\n    let sceneStartTime = performance.now();\n\n    const palette = [\n\n      {\n\n        name: 'cyan',\n\n        r: 0,\n\n        g: 240,\n\n        b: 255,\n\n        glow: 'rgba(0,240,255,0.7)',\n\n        maxAlpha: 0.95\n\n      },\n\n      {\n\n        name: 'pink',\n\n        r: 255,\n\n        g: 0,\n\n        b: 127,\n\n        glow: 'rgba(255,0,127,0.7)',\n\n        maxAlpha: 0.95\n\n      },\n\n      {\n\n        name: 'purple',\n\n        r: 94,\n\n        g: 0,\n\n        b: 180,\n\n        glow: 'rgba(94,0,180,0.55)',\n\n        maxAlpha: 0.72\n\n      },\n\n      {\n\n        name: 'blue',\n\n        r: 46,\n\n        g: 93,\n\n        b: 255,\n\n        glow: 'rgba(46,93,255,0.55)',\n\n        maxAlpha: 0.76\n\n      }\n\n    ];\n\n    function resize() {\n\n      width = window.innerWidth;\n\n      height = window.innerHeight;\n\n      canvas.width = width;\n\n      canvas.height = height;\n\n      if (started) {\n\n        resetPhysicsScene();\n\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    function createBoundary(x, y, w, h, options = {}) {\n\n      const body = Bodies.rectangle(x, y, w, h, {\n\n        isStatic: true,\n\n        friction: 0.8,\n\n        restitution: 0.1,\n\n        ...options\n\n      });\n\n      boundaries.push(body);\n\n      World.add(world, body);\n\n      return body;\n\n    }\n\n    function createPixelBody(x, y, size, color, index, options = {}) {\n\n      const body = Bodies.rectangle(x, y, size, size, {\n\n        restitution: 0.26,\n\n        friction: 0.74,\n\n        frictionStatic: 0.85,\n\n        frictionAir: 0.012,\n\n        density: 0.0035,\n\n        chamfer: {\n\n          radius: 1\n\n        },\n\n        sleepThreshold: 42,\n\n        ...options\n\n      });\n\n      Body.setAngularVelocity(body, (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.18);\n\n      Body.setVelocity(body, {\n\n        x: (Math.random() - 0.5) * 2.8,\n\n        y: Math.random() * 1.8\n\n      });\n\n      return {\n\n        body,\n\n        size,\n\n        color,\n\n        index,\n\n        alpha: Math.random() * color.maxAlpha,\n\n        targetAlpha: Math.random() * color.maxAlpha,\n\n        maxAlpha: color.maxAlpha,\n\n        flickerSpeed: Math.random() * 0.035 + 0.012,\n\n        blinkOffset: Math.random() * Math.PI * 2,\n\n        settled: false\n\n      };\n\n    }\n\n    function initPhysics() {\n\n      engine = Engine.create({\n\n        enableSleeping: true\n\n      });\n\n      world = engine.world;\n\n      world.gravity.x = 0;\n\n      world.gravity.y = 1.15;\n\n      runner = Runner.create();\n\n      Runner.run(runner, engine);\n\n    }\n\n    function buildPhysicsStage() {\n\n      boundaries.length = 0;\n\n      // Floor.\n\n      createBoundary(width / 2, height + 40, width + 400, 80);\n\n      // Walls.\n\n      createBoundary(-80, height / 2, 120, height * 2);\n\n      createBoundary(width + 80, height / 2, 120, height * 2);\n\n      // Bottom-right invisible ramp, so cubes pile toward the visual arcade terrain area.\n\n      const ramp = Bodies.rectangle(width * 0.72, height * 0.88, width * 0.82, 34, {\n\n        isStatic: true,\n\n        angle: -0.28,\n\n        friction: 0.92,\n\n        restitution: 0.05\n\n      });\n\n      boundaries.push(ramp);\n\n      World.add(world, ramp);\n\n    }\n\n    function spawnFallingPixels() {\n\n      blocks.length = 0;\n\n      delayedBodies.length = 0;\n\n      const isMobile = width < 768;\n\n      const count = isMobile ? 75 : 145;\n\n      const firstWaveCount = Math.floor(count * 0.64);\n\n      for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n\n        const color = palette[Math.floor(Math.random() * palette.length)];\n\n        // First wave lands mostly right side.\n\n        // Delayed wave intentionally falls closer to the headline, so it can bounce off words.\n\n        const isDelayed = i >= firstWaveCount;\n\n        const spawnMinX = isMobile\n\n          ? width * 0.12\n\n          : isDelayed\n\n            ? width * 0.06\n\n            : width * 0.48;\n\n        const spawnMaxX = isMobile\n\n          ? width * 0.95\n\n          : isDelayed\n\n            ? width * 0.58\n\n            : width * 0.98;\n\n        const x = spawnMinX + Math.random() * (spawnMaxX - spawnMinX);\n\n        const y = isDelayed\n\n          ? -160 - Math.random() * 360\n\n          : -80 - Math.random() * height * 0.9 - i * 1.4;\n\n        const sizeVariation = Math.random();\n\n        const size =\n\n          sizeVariation > 0.88 ? blockSize * 1.35 :\n\n          sizeVariation > 0.62 ? blockSize * 1.1 :\n\n          blockSize;\n\n        const block = createPixelBody(x, y, size, color, i, {\n\n          isStatic: isDelayed\n\n        });\n\n        blocks.push(block);\n\n        if (isDelayed) {\n\n          delayedBodies.push(block.body);\n\n        }\n\n        World.add(world, block.body);\n\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    function createWordColliders() {\n\n      if (!world || wordCollidersCreated) return;\n\n      // Remove older word colliders first.\n\n      if (wordColliderBodies.length) {\n\n        World.remove(world, wordColliderBodies);\n\n        wordColliderBodies.length = 0;\n\n      }\n\n      const wordEls = document.querySelectorAll('.word-collider');\n\n      wordEls.forEach((el, index) => {\n\n        const rect = el.getBoundingClientRect();\n\n        // Ignore invisible or tiny rects.\n\n        if (rect.width < 8 || rect.height < 8) return;\n\n        const centerX = rect.left + rect.width / 2;\n\n        const centerY = rect.top + rect.height / 2;\n\n        // Slightly smaller than visual text so cubes feel like they hit the actual glyph mass,\n\n        // not an oversized invisible wall.\n\n        const colliderWidth = rect.width * 0.88;\n\n        const colliderHeight = rect.height * 0.68;\n\n        const body = Bodies.rectangle(centerX, centerY, colliderWidth, colliderHeight, {\n\n          isStatic: true,\n\n          restitution: 0.34,\n\n          friction: 0.18,\n\n          frictionStatic: 0.2,\n\n          label: `word-collider-${index}`,\n\n          render: {\n\n            visible: false\n\n          }\n\n        });\n\n        wordColliderBodies.push(body);\n\n      });\n\n      World.add(world, wordColliderBodies);\n\n      wordCollidersCreated = true;\n\n      // Remove word colliders after enough time so cubes eventually fall fully into the canvas pile.\n\n      // This prevents the text from permanently trapping blocks above the hero.\n\n      setTimeout(() => {\n\n        if (world && wordColliderBodies.length) {\n\n          World.remove(world, wordColliderBodies);\n\n          wordColliderBodies.length = 0;\n\n          wordCollidersCreated = false;\n\n        }\n\n      }, 5200);\n\n    }\n\n    function releaseDelayedWave() {\n\n      if (delayedWaveReleased) return;\n\n      delayedWaveReleased = true;\n\n      delayedBodies.forEach((body, index) => {\n\n        setTimeout(() => {\n\n          Body.setStatic(body, false);\n\n          Body.setVelocity(body, {\n\n            x: 0.8 + Math.random() * 2.4,\n\n            y: 1.5 + Math.random() * 2.2\n\n          });\n\n          Body.setAngularVelocity(body, (Math.random() - 0.5) * 0.22);\n\n          Sleeping.set(body, false);\n\n        }, index * 28);\n\n      });\n\n    }\n\n    function resetPhysicsScene() {\n\n      if (runner) {\n\n        Runner.stop(runner);\n\n      }\n\n      if (engine) {\n\n        World.clear(world, false);\n\n        Engine.clear(engine);\n\n      }\n\n      initPhysics();\n\n      buildPhysicsStage();\n\n      spawnFallingPixels();\n\n      physicsActive = true;\n\n      settleTimer = null;\n\n      wordCollidersCreated = false;\n\n      delayedWaveReleased = false;\n\n      wordColliderBodies.length = 0;\n\n      sceneStartTime = performance.now();\n\n      // If the headline has already revealed, recreate word colliders after resize.\n\n      setTimeout(() => {\n\n        createWordColliders();\n\n        releaseDelayedWave();\n\n      }, 900);\n\n    }\n\n    function averageMotion() {\n\n      if (!blocks.length) return Infinity;\n\n      let total = 0;\n\n      blocks.forEach(block => {\n\n        const v = block.body.velocity;\n\n        total += Math.abs(v.x) + Math.abs(v.y) + Math.abs(block.body.angularVelocity);\n\n      });\n\n      return total / blocks.length;\n\n    }\n\n    function checkSettled() {\n\n      if (!physicsActive) return;\n\n      const elapsed = performance.now() - sceneStartTime;\n\n      const elapsedEnough = elapsed > 4800;\n\n      const lowMotion = averageMotion() < 0.08;\n\n      if (elapsedEnough && lowMotion) {\n\n        if (!settleTimer) {\n\n          settleTimer = setTimeout(() => {\n\n            freezePile();\n\n          }, 900);\n\n        }\n\n      } else {\n\n        settleTimer = null;\n\n      }\n\n      // Fallback freeze so the physics engine doesn't run forever.\n\n      if (elapsed > 9800) {\n\n        freezePile();\n\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    function freezePile() {\n\n      if (!physicsActive) return;\n\n      physicsActive = false;\n\n      if (wordColliderBodies.length) {\n\n        World.remove(world, wordColliderBodies);\n\n        wordColliderBodies.length = 0;\n\n      }\n\n      blocks.forEach(block => {\n\n        block.settled = true;\n\n        Sleeping.set(block.body, true);\n\n        Body.setStatic(block.body, true);\n\n      });\n\n      if (runner) {\n\n        Runner.stop(runner);\n\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    function drawBlock(block, time) {\n\n      const body = block.body;\n\n      const pos = body.position;\n\n      const angle = body.angle;\n\n      const size = block.size;\n\n      const color = block.color;\n\n      // Continue blinking after physics is settled.\n\n      const blinkPulse = Math.sin(time * 0.002 + block.blinkOffset) * 0.18 + 0.82;\n\n      block.alpha += (block.targetAlpha - block.alpha) * block.flickerSpeed;\n\n      if (Math.abs(block.alpha - block.targetAlpha) < 0.025) {\n\n        block.targetAlpha = (0.22 + Math.random() * 0.78) * block.maxAlpha;\n\n      }\n\n      const alpha = Math.max(0.08, block.alpha * blinkPulse);\n\n      ctx.save();\n\n      ctx.translate(pos.x, pos.y);\n\n      ctx.rotate(angle);\n\n      // Neon outer glow.\n\n      ctx.shadowBlur = 16;\n\n      ctx.shadowColor = color.glow;\n\n      // Main pixel face.\n\n      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${color.r}, ${color.g}, ${color.b}, ${alpha})`;\n\n      ctx.fillRect(-size / 2, -size / 2, size - 2, size - 2);\n\n      // Beveled top edge.\n\n      ctx.shadowBlur = 0;\n\n      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(255, 255, 255, ${alpha * 0.32})`;\n\n      ctx.fillRect(-size / 2, -size / 2, size - 2, 3);\n\n      // Dark lower bevel.\n\n      ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(0, 0, 0, ${alpha * 0.44})`;\n\n      ctx.fillRect(-size / 2, size / 2 - 5, size - 2, 3);\n\n      // Inner pixel inset.\n\n      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(255, 255, 255, ${alpha * 0.10})`;\n\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n\n      ctx.strokeRect(-size / 2 + 3, -size / 2 + 3, size - 8, size - 8);\n\n      ctx.restore();\n\n    }\n\n    function drawBackgroundBase() {\n\n      ctx.fillStyle = '#050010';\n\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n      // Background radial color wash.\n\n      const gradient = ctx.createRadialGradient(\n\n        width * 0.78,\n\n        height * 0.38,\n\n        0,\n\n        width * 0.78,\n\n        height * 0.38,\n\n        Math.max(width, height) * 0.72\n\n      );\n\n      gradient.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.13)');\n\n      gradient.addColorStop(0.35, 'rgba(255, 0, 127, 0.08)');\n\n      gradient.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(5, 0, 16, 0)');\n\n      ctx.fillStyle = gradient;\n\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n      // Distant static terrain for depth.\n\n      const gridSize = 32;\n\n      const columns = Math.ceil(width / gridSize);\n\n      const rows = Math.ceil(height / gridSize);\n\n      for (let c = 0; c < columns; c++) {\n\n        const normalizedX = c / columns;\n\n        const curve = Math.pow(normalizedX, 3.8);\n\n        const startRow = rows - Math.floor(rows * curve * 0.55);\n\n        for (let r = startRow; r < rows; r++) {\n\n          if (Math.random() > 0.985) {\n\n            ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.05)';\n\n            ctx.fillRect(c * gridSize, r * gridSize, gridSize - 2, gridSize - 2);\n\n          }\n\n        }\n\n      }\n\n    }\n\n    function animatePixels(time) {\n\n      drawBackgroundBase();\n\n      blocks.forEach(block => {\n\n        drawBlock(block, time);\n\n      });\n\n      checkSettled();\n\n      requestAnimationFrame(animatePixels);\n\n    }\n\n    window.addEventListener('resize', resize);\n\n    resize();\n\n    resetPhysicsScene();\n\n    started = true;\n\n    requestAnimationFrame(animatePixels);\n\n  </script>\n\n</body>\n\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "nexus-ready-player-one.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmv